From: Omarchy Mobile <omamobile@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: msm8953: add a system power domain above the clusters

The deepest domain state is cluster power collapse, so in s2idle the
CPUs and both clusters power down but the apps subsystem never hands
off to RPM: on a Redmi 4 Prime the RPM master stats show APSS with zero
shutdowns after a 96-minute s2idle, and the RPM sleep stats show no
XO shutdown (vlow) or VDD minimisation (vmin) at all.

The vendor kernel's low-power levels have a third, system level above
the two clusters (the CCI SPM, PSCI mode field at bit 8), whose power
collapse (mode 3) is the one that notifies RPM. Add it as a parent
power domain of cluster0 and cluster1 with that state: CPU mode 3,
cluster mode 5, system mode 3, power-down bit, affinity level 2.

The firmware runs in OS-initiated mode, so the last CPU down passes the
composite state of the highest domain that powers off.

---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8953.dtsi | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8953.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8953.dtsi
@@ -280,6 +280,16 @@
 				min-residency-us = <2500>;
 				local-timer-stop;
 			};
+
+			system_pc: system-power-collapse {
+				compatible = "domain-idle-state";
+				idle-state-name = "system-pc";
+				arm,psci-suspend-param = <0x42000353>;
+				entry-latency-us = <1500>;
+				exit-latency-us = <11000>;
+				min-residency-us = <100000>;
+				local-timer-stop;
+			};
 		};
 
 		l2_0: l2-cache-0 {
@@ -597,11 +607,18 @@
 		cluster0_pd: power-domain-cluster0 {
 			#power-domain-cells = <0>;
 			domain-idle-states = <&cluster_ret>, <&cluster_gdhs>, <&cluster_pc>;
+			power-domains = <&system_pd>;
 		};
 
 		cluster1_pd: power-domain-cluster1 {
 			#power-domain-cells = <0>;
 			domain-idle-states = <&cluster_ret>, <&cluster_gdhs>, <&cluster_pc>;
+			power-domains = <&system_pd>;
+		};
+
+		system_pd: power-domain-system {
+			#power-domain-cells = <0>;
+			domain-idle-states = <&system_pc>;
 		};
 	};
 
